  "notes": "- **Include subfolders is now an option, and off by default.** Choosing a folder used to take every folder inside it as well. In a folder that keeps earlier output in a subfolder (`converted/`, say), that queued the output too. The checkbox appears in three places:\n  - in the Queue menu, beside *Choose a folder\u2026*;\n  - in the app settings;\n  - next to the folder notice whenever a folder is queued.\n\n  Changing it rescans the queued folder.\n- *Recreate folder structure* only applies when subfolders are included.\n\nIf you are on 0.8.0 or later, the app offers this update itself.\n\nInstallers: Linux `.deb` and AppImage, Windows `x64-setup.exe`, and macOS `.dmg` for Apple Silicon and Intel. CI attaches each one as its platform finishes. The `.sig` files and `latest.json` next to them are for the updater."
